# Personal Obsidian vault content — never public.
#
# This rule named only "Personal Intelligence/" until the vault was renamed on
# disk to "Praxis iIntelligence", at which point the pattern quietly stopped
# matching and 387 files of private research sat untracked in a public repo,
# one `git add -A` away from being pushed. Nothing leaked (checked: zero
# commits touch it in any branch). Then it happened AGAIN on the rename to
# "Praxis Intelligence". Renames are the failure mode, so this now matches on
# shape rather than on any one spelling: any top-level "* Intelligence/" folder
# is personal-vault content and never belongs in this repo.
*Intelligence/
Personal Intelligence/
.obsidian/

# hyperframes clone (local tool, not part of praxis)
hyperframes/
videos/
